#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139340} :activity/id #uuid "0f1320ae-5783-5e37-b1a5-3098937007e1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049943 :topic/id #uuid "202bf905-577e-51ee-b1b6-25f29f3d77aa" :topic/math-academy-id 2275} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139340 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139725 :tutorial/content "The **difference of squares formula** states the product of the sum and the difference of two monomials is equal to the difference of their squares:\n\n$$\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$\n\nWe can check that this result is correct by expanding the binomial in the usual way, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t({\\color{blue}a} + {\\color{red}b})(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t{\\color{blue}a}(a - b) + {\\color{red}b}(a - b) &= \\[5pt]\n\t\ta^2 - ab + ab - b^2 &= \\[5pt]\n\t\ta^2 - b^2 \\,& {\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n\t}\n$$\n\nNotice that the middle two terms $- ab$ and $ab$ cancel each other out, leaving only $a^2 - b^2.$ \n\nIf the order of multiplication is switched, the formula still remains the same:\n\n$$\n(a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "5aaa853f-8b04-5d91-8c05-f30646908746" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8883 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "3d09b7a5-02a2-5bb1-ab6c-97fd9a0d593c" :step/math-academy-id 193358 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139341}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139341 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138420 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138186 :question/id #uuid "6d8e25fc-b9a0-5cd1-9a33-3e7c6d34d2c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-14323"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08fda5c2-ae08-54fe-8271-b2f4c1f92eb1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050818}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138749} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138773} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483376} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483403} {:db/i